1. Valence issues: closely linked to governing competence, this is where voters decide based n who they think is most likely to run the country effectively, specially when it comes to the economy
2. Rational choice: voting based on self-interest, i.e. the voter studying the manifestos and calculating what they can gain personally by voting a particular way - i.e. based on logic, not emotion
3. Issue voting: the idea that each voter will have **one main issue** (e.g. Brexit; pensions) or even **one event** (e.g. Manchester Arena Bombing 2017; Falklands war 1983) that they care about, and will voted based on the parties’ policies on that specific issue
    - Usually based more on emotion than logic
